  "title": "Chile’s Pinochet-era soldier jailed for killing folk singer Victor Jara",
  "summary": "Chile’s military coup in 1973 led to Nelson Haase being convicted of the murder of Victor Jara, a folk singer, after the coup. The conviction and subsequent trial, which took place over 53 years, resulted in Haase being sentenced to life in prison.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Nelson Haase was convicted of murdering Victor Jara in 2023 after the military coup in Chile.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Haase was sentenced to life in prison for the crime and fled from authorities in 2023.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The event highlights a connection to Pinochet’s legacy and the ongoing conflict over the murder of a national figure.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
